+[[gcode:g10-l3]]
+== G10 L3 Set Tool Wear Offset(((G10 L3 Tool Wear Offset)))
+
+[source,ngc]
+----
+G10 L3 P- axes
+----
+
+G10 L3 replaces the supplied absolute wear values for an existing nonzero
+tool. Omitted axes remain unchanged and an explicit zero clears that wear
+axis. Values use ordinary program-unit conversion; X also follows G7/G8
+diameter/radius interpretation. R, I, J, and Q are not allowed.
+
+[source,ngc]
+----
+G10 L3 P7 X0.050 Z-0.010
+----
+
+The tool table is persisted, but an active motion offset is not changed
+until G43 is executed or the tool is changed again.
+
 [[gcode:g10-l2]]
 == G10 L2 Set Coordinate System(((G10 L2 Coordinate System)))
 
@@ -1404,7 +1427,8 @@ G43 <H->
 
 'G43' without an H word uses the currently loaded tool from the last 'T__n__ M6'.
 
-'G43 H__n__' uses the offset for tool _n_.
+'G43 H__n__' uses the sum of the geometry and wear offsets for tool _n_
+on all nine axes. Repeating G43 replaces the active value and is idempotent.
 
 The active tool length compensation values are stored in the numbered
 parameters '5401-5409'.
@@ -1473,7 +1497,7 @@ G43.2 H- or axes-
 
 * 'H' - tool number
 
-* 'G43.2 H__n__' - applies an additional simultaneous tool offset to subsequent motions by adding the offset(s) of tool _n_.
+* 'G43.2 H__n__' - applies an additional simultaneous tool offset to subsequent motions by adding the geometry plus wear offset(s) of tool _n_.
 
 * 'G43.2 axes' - applies an additional simultaneous tool offset to subsequent motions by adding the value(s) of any axis words.
 
@@ -1497,10 +1521,8 @@ G43.2 X0.01 Z0.02 (also add 0.01 to the x tool offset and 0.02 to the z tool off
 M2 (end program)
 ----
 
-You can sum together an arbitrary number of offsets by calling G43.2
-more times.  There are no built-in assumptions about which numbers are
-geometry offsets and which are wear offsets, or that you should have
-only one of each.
+You can sum together an arbitrary number of independent offsets by calling
+G43.2 more times.
 
 Like the other G43 commands, G43.2 does not cause any motion. The next
 time a compensated axis is moved, that axis's endpoint is the compensated location.
@@ -1516,7 +1538,9 @@ NOTE: G43.2 does not write to the tool table.
 [[gcode:g49]]
 == G49 Cancel Tool Length Compensation(((G49 Cancel Tool Length Offset)))
 
-* 'G49' - cancels tool length compensation
+* 'G49' - cancels the complete active tool length compensation without
+  changing stored geometry or wear. It remains cancelled until G43 or a
+  subsequent built-in tool change.
 
 It is OK to program using the same offset already in use. It is also
 OK to program using no tool length offset if none is currently being
